-- ============================================================================
-- DR10 ASSOCIATE DEEP SEED: Stimulation Design, beginner tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: the two answers to two different problems. If the well
-- is DAMAGED, the near wellbore is the problem and acid clears it. If the well
-- is merely TIGHT, the reservoir is the problem and a fracture goes around it.
-- Skin, the Hawkins formula, both acid routes, and the rate ceiling a matrix
-- job must stay under.
--
-- THE SHAPE THE TIER IS BUILT ON. Damage is described by TWO numbers and the
-- skin depends on them in completely different ways: LINEARLY on the
-- permeability contrast and only LOGARITHMICALLY on the damaged radius. So
-- severe damage is expensive and deep damage is comparatively cheap, and a
-- single measured skin never fixes the pair. What follows for design is that
-- treating a severe shallow ring is worth far more per cubic metre than
-- chasing a mild deep one.
--
-- THE SECOND SHAPE, AND IT RUNS THE OTHER WAY. An acid planning volume grows
-- with the SQUARE of the target radius while the benefit grows only with its
-- logarithm. Benefit logarithmic, cost quadratic, running in opposite
-- directions, which is the whole economics of a matrix job in one sentence.
-- The published plan reaches only two thirds of the way to the damage and
-- leaves a residual skin, and the engine is unusually blunt about it: the
-- residual is a STEP on whether the front reached the damaged radius, so a job
-- that stops short earns no partial credit proportional to spend.
--
-- THE TRAP THIS TIER PAID FOR. The matrix rate ceiling takes the viscosity of
-- the ACID, near 1e-3 Pa.s, and NOT the fracturing fluid's. A first draft of
-- the teaching lab passed the frac fluid's gel viscosity and understated the
-- ceiling by a factor of two hundred, which makes a routine job look
-- impossible. The lab now asserts that ratio explicitly. And because skin sits
-- in the DENOMINATOR of the ceiling, the damaged well you are trying to treat
-- is exactly the well that accepts acid most slowly, which turns a physics
-- remark into a scheduling and cost argument.
-- ============================================================================

values ('stimulation', 'beginner', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-what-this-course-decides","title":"What This Course Decides","lesson_keys":["l01-two-ways-to-stimulate","l02-matrix-or-fracture","l03-what-this-engine-models","l04-what-it-refuses"]},{"key":"m02-damage-and-what-it-costs","title":"Damage, and What It Costs","lesson_keys":["l01-skin-in-one-paragraph","l02-hawkins","l03-a-ratio-and-a-radius","l04-which-one-moves-the-skin","l05-a-measured-skin-is-a-sum"]},{"key":"m03-the-acid-route","title":"The Acid Route","lesson_keys":["l01-sandstone-and-carbonate-are-different-jobs","l02-the-pore-volume-idea","l03-planning-a-sandstone-volume","l04-when-the-acid-stops-short","l05-the-volume-is-not-the-answer"]},{"key":"m04-carbonates-and-wormholes","title":"Carbonates and Wormholes","lesson_keys":["l01-a-wormhole-is-not-dissolution","l02-the-wormhole-radius","l03-pore-volumes-to-breakthrough","l04-the-skin-a-wormhole-gives","l05-why-the-two-routes-differ"]},{"key":"m05-the-matrix-ceiling","title":"The Matrix Ceiling","lesson_keys":["l01-below-frac-pressure-or-it-is-not-matrix","l02-the-darcy-ceiling","l03-what-the-ceiling-depends-on","l04-damage-lowers-the-ceiling"]},{"key":"m06-the-associate-reading","title":"The Associate Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-story-so-far","l02-working-the-capstone","l03-onward"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
